{
  "_read_me": "Four-part parity registry, enforced by tests/test_feature_parity.py (owner rule 2026-10-06: the Python package, the MCP server, the desktop exe and the web site each have every feature). Every public name of the library (every __all__ entry, every MCP tool, every phase rule, every CLI command) is listed exactly once: under a feature, which must name at least one library function, at least one MCP tool and working app evidence (the desktop exe is the web app in a shell); under 'internal' with the reason it needs no surface; or under 'deferred' with the owner's dated decision. A new public name fails CI until it is listed here, and every feature's evidence (DOM ids in web/index.html, bridge methods the front end calls, exported browser-core functions the page uses, tests that exist) is checked on every run.",
